{
  "summary": "Switches signature-cache key hashing to native HashWriter serialization so ECDSA public keys and signatures include CompactSize length prefixes. Precomputes immutable salted hasher prefixes using single-byte domain tags without block padding, and changes the public ComputeEntry methods to return entry digests by value. Adds a constructor that accepts an explicit nonce to facilitate deterministic testing, along with expanded unit and fuzz tests comparing cached against uncached verification.",
  "problem": "Signature-cache key generation previously concatenated raw byte buffers without length prefixes, relying on implicit assumptions: ECDSA public key headers delimit key length, and Schnorr inputs have fixed sizes. While secure under current script checker validation rules, un-delimited byte stream hashing is fragile against future script extensions and mirrors the pattern behind a vulnerability and exploit in the Elements rangeproof cache.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description points directly to the Elements rangeproof-cache vulnerability behind the Liquid network security incident and Elements PR #1600 as the motivation to eliminate un-delimited raw byte hashing.",
    "PR description: 'Bitcoin Core's signature-cache encoding is unambiguous for inputs accepted by its current script checker: a valid ECDSA public key's prefix determines its length, while a Schnorr public key is always 32 bytes, leaving the signature as the remaining suffix.'"
  ],
