  "changed_since_previous": "Rather than keeping cache key bytes identical, the PR now alters the internal cache key serialization: ECDSA keys and signatures are serialized with CompactSize length prefixes, the 32-byte salted hasher prefix padding is removed in favor of a one-byte type discriminator, and an explicit nonce constructor is added for tests.",
  "card": "Switches signature-cache key derivation to native HashWriter serialization, prepending CompactSize lengths to ECDSA public keys and signatures to ensure unambiguous key boundaries. The change addresses an implicit input requirement where cache keys hashed raw concatenated byte spans without length framing, an un-delimited pattern inspired by an exploit in Elements' rangeproof cache during the Liquid security incident. Cache digests are now returned by value, salted prefixes are simplified, and deterministic cache testing is enabled via a nonce-taking constructor. The cache is entirely process-local and consensus rules are unchanged, though any bug in cache keys directly affects script verification.",
